            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous dissection of the splanchnic arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>656-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1510/icvts.2009.219907</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three patients had severe abdominal pain of sudden onset. Computed tomography showed localized dissection in the superior mesenteric artery in two patients and in the celiac artery in one. With conservative therapy abdominal symptoms were self-remitted. All patients were successfully treated with medication and have been doing well during follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
